1517-Conclusion
1518-
1519-We have presented a novel framework for demanded abstract
1520-interpretation, in which an arbitrary abstract interpretation
1521-can be made both incremental and demand-driven. Unlike
1522-previous frameworks, ours supports arbitrary lattices and
1523-widening operators. The framework is based on a novel demanded abstract interpretation graph (DAIG) representation
1524-of the analysis problem, where careful handling of loops
1525:ensures the DAIG remains acyclic. We have proved various key properties of the framework, including soundness,
1526-termination, and from-scratch consistency. Our implementation shows that complex analyses can be easily implemented
1527-with our framework, with the potential for significant performance wins in incremental and demand-driven scenarios.
